.", "Heavy alcohol use moderately supports acute pancreatic catastrophe (B4), but absence of back pain and elevated amylase/lipase weakens this link."], "evidence_against": ["The gradual onset with acute exacerbation during exercise moderately argues against gynecologic/pelvic catastrophe (B1) but remains compatible with chronic-to-acute hepatic vascular processes."], "unresolved_questions": [], "askable_discriminators": ["History of amenorrhea or missed period", "Vaginal bleeding or spotting", "Pelvic examination findings (e.g., tenderness, masses)"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Pelvic ultrasound for hemoperitoneum or adnexal mass", "Qualitative β-hCG confirmation", "Complete blood count for anemia"]}, "target_level": 2}
